WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.037
Step three lists the
permissions the read needs.

2
00:00:03.037 --> 00:00:07.450
Four: Group dot Read Basic dot All,
and the three PIM for Groups reads,

3
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:12.825
for assignment schedules, eligibility
schedules and role management policies.

4
00:00:12.825 --> 00:00:14.500
Nothing ends in ReadWrite.

5
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:18.413
Step four plans against the
fictional tenant, as a dry run.

6
00:00:18.413 --> 00:00:20.597
You give it the cloud, the fixture,

7
00:00:20.597 --> 00:00:24.075
the desired state file, the
date and an output folder.

8
00:00:24.075 --> 00:00:27.562
The read raises nine
findings and three warnings.

9
00:00:27.562 --> 00:00:30.659
The plan has eight changes:
three assignments,

10
00:00:30.659 --> 00:00:33.512
two eligibilities and three policy rules.

11
00:00:33.512 --> 00:00:36.638
The guards all passed, so
the plan could be applied.

12
00:00:36.638 --> 00:00:39.071
But it's a dry run, so nothing was sent:

13
00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:42.820
review the diff and the plan,
then run again with Apply.
